      "title": "clarify-gate-guarantees",
      "type": "epic",
      "priority": 1,
      "pinned": true,
      "description": "Make every claim this repository makes about what a gate guarantees match what the gate actually does, and record what the instructions were verified against so a reader can tell a verified instruction from a plausible one.",
      "acceptance_criteria": "No gate type is described in terms stronger than its behaviour: a human gate is a record of a decision any caller can make, a GitHub gate reports an error rather than closing when it cannot be evaluated, and the type known to fail when evaluated is named as such. The schema README carries a verification baseline with versions, a date, and the behaviours measured rather than assumed, plus a note wherever an instruction deliberately differs from upstream documentation.",
      "labels": ["openspec", "change:clarify-gate-guarantees"]
    },
